# Gatekeep — build and test

## Tool paths (workspace `.tools/`)

JDK and the Android SDK are **not** on global PATH. They live under the **Private workspace root** (`../.tools/` from `Gatekeep/`):

| Tool | Path |
|------|------|
| **JDK 17** | `c:/Users/JimBuisman/Desktop/Private/.tools/jdk-17.0.14+7` |
| **Android SDK** | `c:/Users/JimBuisman/Desktop/Private/.tools/android-sdk` |

`Gatekeep/local.properties` already points `sdk.dir` at the Android SDK.

Before Gradle, set:

```bash
export JAVA_HOME="c:/Users/JimBuisman/Desktop/Private/.tools/jdk-17.0.14+7"
export ANDROID_HOME="c:/Users/JimBuisman/Desktop/Private/.tools/android-sdk"
```

From `Gatekeep/`:

```bash
cd Gatekeep
export JAVA_HOME="c:/Users/JimBuisman/Desktop/Private/.tools/jdk-17.0.14+7"
export ANDROID_HOME="c:/Users/JimBuisman/Desktop/Private/.tools/android-sdk"
./gradlew :core-domain:test :core-data:test :app:testDebugUnitTest :app:assembleRelease
```

**Prerequisite:** `keystore/debug.keystore` must exist (one-time setup below). Without it, release builds are unsigned.

APK output: `app/build/outputs/apk/release/app-release.apk` (arm64-v8a only; see `app/build.gradle.kts` `abiFilters`).

One-time keystore setup (from `Gatekeep/`):

```bash
mkdir -p keystore
"$JAVA_HOME/bin/keytool" -genkeypair -v -keystore keystore/debug.keystore -alias androiddebugkey \
  -keyalg RSA -keysize 2048 -validity 10000 -storepass android -keypass android \
  -dname "CN=Gatekeep Debug, OU=Dev, O=Gatekeep, L=Local, ST=Local, C=NL"
```

Release and debug both sign with `debugShared` (`keystore/debug.keystore`, passwords `android`). The keystore is gitignored — each machine needs its own copy, or copy the file once to keep upgrade compatibility.

## Requirements

- JDK 17
- Android SDK 35 (installed in `.tools/android-sdk`)

## Notes

- Room schema bumps require an explicit `Migration` in `core-data` — do **not** use `fallbackToDestructiveMigration()` (profiles would be wiped on upgrade).
- Do not assume `java` or `adb` are on PATH; use the paths above or `local.properties`.
